%% NREM spindle-triggered neuronal firing rate analysis
% This script separates recorded neuronal spike trains into thalamic and
% hippocampal populations based on shank location and removes thalamic
% cells with low NREM firing rates.
%
% Neuronal spike activity is aligned to detected global and local sleep
% spindle events using the corresponding representative reference channel.
% For each spindle type, spike rasters and peri-spindle firing-rate profiles
% are generated within a +/-0.5 s window around the spindle peak, and the
% firing rates are smoothed using a Gaussian kernel.
%
% The firing-rate modulation of each cell is quantified by calculating the
% absolute difference between the maximum firing-rate peak and the minimum
% trough within a restricted spindle-centered time window. These modulation
% indices are calculated separately for global and local spindles.
%
% The resulting individual-cell firing-rate profiles, spike rasters, and
% modulation indices are stored separately for global and local spindles.
% Representative spindle-related EEG signals, spike rasters, and firing
% rate profiles are plotted for individual cells.
%
% The processed firing-rate data, spike rasters, modulation indices, and
% NREM spike trains are saved as MAT files, and all generated figures are
% exported in both PNG and MATLAB FIG formats.

